{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_entity_hierarchy", "label": "Entity hierarchy (parent/child)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_two_hierarchies_principle", "label": "Two hierarchies, two responsibilities", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nexus owns structure (transform-agnostic), gameplay owns transform composition, and the render bridge keeps nebula nodes flat \u2014 the Bevy split. Routing entity structure through the nebula SceneGraph would make the editor and physics depend on the renderer."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_parent_component", "label": "Parent component", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The relation is stored as data (hence queryable and serializable); Parent is carried by the child and roots are found with query(...).without(Parent)."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_children_component", "label": "Children component", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "API-maintained and read-only outside; getChildren returns the LIVE array (not a defensive copy) typed ReadonlyArray, so it must not be mutated nor retained across setParent/destroyEntity."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_setparent_api", "label": "world.setParent / getParent / getChildren", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Updates both sides atomically, throws on cycles, is idempotent, and destroys descendants recursively by default (Unity style); reparenting inside a query().each() is structural and must go through world.commands.setParent."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_mat3_completion", "label": "Mat3 completion (multiply / invert / decompose)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Makes Mat3 a full 2D affine matrix (useful for physics, rendering and editor gizmos) and avoids dragging Mat4's 16 floats where 9 suffice; matrix composition is exact under shear where naive TRS composition is approximate. invert is what powers worldPositionStays."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_worldtransform2d", "label": "WorldTransform2D", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Transform2D becomes the LOCAL transform (backwards compatible while everything is a root) and WorldTransform2D carries the derived world matrix, created and removed automatically by propagation."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_transformpropagationsystem", "label": "TransformPropagationSystem", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Walks roots\u2192leaves so a parent is always computed before its children; a dynamic body ignores parent composition (physics is authority) but its children still compose on its world. V1 recomputes the whole tree each frame."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_worldpositionstays", "label": "worldPositionStays reparent semantics", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defaults to true like Unity: local = parentWorld.invert() * currentWorld is recomputed so the world pose does not move; with false the local is reinterpreted in the new frame and the child snaps."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_shear_caveat", "label": "Lossy TRS decomposition at the render edge", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The flat SpriteNode consumes TRS, not a matrix, so the world matrix is decomposed \u2014 exact everywhere except a sheared quad (non-uniform parent scale + nested rotation), the same tradeoff as Unity's lossyScale. Physics is rigid so it is always exact."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_one_frame_physics_latency", "label": "One-frame physics latency", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Propagation sits at the end of the update lane, so render reads a fresh world transform the same frame while fixed/PhysicsRequest reads last frame's \u2014 exactly the latency physics already tolerates. Pure visual children (health bars, weapons, decor) are 100% exact."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_physicspull_dynamic_restriction", "label": "PhysicsPull restricted to dynamic bodies", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Writing body world into Transform2D for every body would overwrite a kinematic/static child's LOCAL transform with WORLD data \u2014 silent corruption; restricting the pull to dynamic is also what the declared authority model demands."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_setparent_api", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_command_buffer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_parent_component", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_query_filters", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_entity_hierarchy", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_nexus_ecs", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_setparent_api", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_fail_fast_guard", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_one_frame_physics_latency", "target": "docs_core_scheduling_stage_vocabulary", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_entity_hierarchy", "target": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_two_hierarchies_principle", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/gameplay/entity-hierarchy.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_two_hierarchies_principle", "target": "docs_gameplay_entity_hierarchy_transformpropagationsystem", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": 